Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage for a 7‑day‑bucket, Monday‑based retention analysis  

• event_date: identifies the calendar day of every event; needed for cohort definition, week bucketing and the ≤ 2018‑10‑02 cut‑off.  
• event_name: lets us pick only the “session_start” events when we determine the user’s 1st visit.  
• user_pseudo_id: stable visitor id; used to tie all events of the same person together.  
• event_timestamp: secondary time stamp (micro‑seconds) in case finer ordering is required.  
• _TABLE_SUFFIX (pseudo‑column when a wildcard table is used): limits the scan to the daily tables that we really need (20180702 … 20181002).

(The other columns exist but are not required for this request.)

